# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The four trees below are NOT lost when they look empty. They are synced
# through the owner's private Dropbox, not through git:
#     python3 tools/data_root.py --status     # what is here vs in the store
#     python3 tools/data_root.py --pull       # materialise them
# Do not hand-copy them. See docs/data-store-coordination_2026-08-14.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Third-party reference implementations — CLUST5 / do_cluster (M. L. Johnson)
# and the Igor Pro Cluster package. We do not have redistribution rights, so
# these are never committed. They ARE in the private store, which is not a
# distribution — and that holds only while the folder stays private. If it is
# ever shared, this tree comes out first. See docs/reference-code.md.
reference/

# Real lab recordings and anything derived from them. Not ours to distribute:
# the app ships simulated data instead (data/synthetic/, tools/make_synthetic.py).
# Unlike reference/ above, these are OURS — gitignored by our choice, not by a
# license. Do not reason about all four trees as one group.
data/extracted/
data/oracle/
data/oracle_igor/
*.pxp

# tools/review_digitization.py's QA page. It embeds CROPS OF THE PUBLISHED
# FIGURE, not just the numbers read off it — the article is not open access,
# data/digitized/README.md declines to redistribute it, and the contractual
# question in docs/figure-data-permissions.md is open. The numbers are
# measurements and travel; the pixels are the publisher's and stay here.
review/

# build/run residue
param_list.Rdata
__pycache__/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
